<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gao Huan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">496–547</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao">Gao</a> Huan was a general of mixed Chinese and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> culture who became the dominant figure in the Northern Wei during its collapse. After destroying the Erzhu clan in 532 he controlled the court; when Emperor Xiaowu fled west in 534, Gao Huan installed a new emperor at Ye, creating the Eastern Wei. He ruled it as regent until his death in 547, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wenxuan-of-northern-qi">Gao Yang</a> founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-qi">Northern Qi</a> in 550.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gao-huan.jpg" alt="Gao Huan" width="320" height="433" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%B8%A4%E6%B5%B7%E7%8E%8B%E9%AB%98%E6%AD%A1%EF%BC%88%E5%8C%97%E5%8F%B2%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%EF%BC%89.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
